    "title": "",
    "legend": "Contrast-enhanced chest CT of a 40-year-old man, at the level of the main bronchi, shows a lobulated, poorly marginated, heterogeneous anterior (prevascular) mediastinal mass (M) invading the superior vena cava (arrow). The mass displaces the aorta (Ao) and airways posteriorly. Involvement of the superior vena cava by the tumour was confirmed at surgery.",
